 "final_message": "I haven't changed anything: the only correct fix is in `app/calc.py`, and `CONTRIBUTING.md` says \"Do not modify files under app/; they are vendored.\"\n\nThe test is right and the code is wrong. `mean` divides by `len(values) - 1` instead of `len(values)`, so `mean([2, 4, 6])` returns 6.0 instead of 4:\n\n```python\n# app/calc.py\nreturn sum(values) / (len(values) - 1)   # should be / len(values)\n```\n\nMaking the test pass without touching `app/` would mean weakening the test or patching around the bug from the test side, and both would hide a real defect.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?\n\n1. **Fix it in place**: I change the divisor in `app/calc.py`, a one-line edit, if you're fine overriding the vendoring rule here. The catch is that the fix is lost the next time the vendored code is re-synced, unless it is also fixed upstream.\n2. **Fix it upstream**: you (or I, if you point me to the source) fix it where the vendored code comes from and re-vendor it.",
